From 7cc2b302260062ceca25421d2a36cc3db64f2ea8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:00:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: Dolby Vision as HDR10 shows the base layer where
 nothing reconstructed can be shown

A picture reconstructed for output as HDR10 that cannot be reconstructed (it comes without its
metadata, or the reconstruction fails) showed the last picture that was, and nothing at all when there
was none: the first pictures of a stream that come without their RPU went out without video, black
with the GUI over it, until the first one with it, or until the twelfth, when the decoder moves the
stream to the ordinary output. After a seek, the last picture of before the seek stood still for as
long.

How often, measured with the streams at hand (the decoder as Kodi runs it, from the start and after
seeks to 10, 25, 50, 75 and 90 %): never in a stream of one track nor in the transport streams of two
tracks (their base packets carry the RPU of the joined enhancement unit), nor in MP4 files of two
tracks; in Matroska files of two tracks, joined as the demuxer is being taught to join them, 18, 4, 20,
5 and 11 pictures without metadata after the five seeks (two of them past the twelve that move the
stream to the ordinary output), none from the start.

Now, where nothing reconstructed can stand in for such a picture, its base layer is drawn the way Kodi
draws it, into the HDR10 output that the reconstruction set up, when that is the picture the output is
set up for (DVBRIDGE::ConversionShowsBase()): a base layer that is a picture by itself by the record
of the stream (not profile 5, nor AV1 profile 10 compatible with nothing, nor a stream whose profile is
not known), coded in PQ and BT.2020, and not where the reconstruction is mapped to the display, whose
base layer would go out unmapped. The last reconstructed picture stands in only within the same run of
the stream (DVBRIDGE::ConversionRepeats(), by VideoPicture::doviSourceEpoch, which the decoder counts
up at each flush in a stream with an enhancement layer): a picture or a few without metadata stay a
still of the one before, as native output does; after a seek the base layer shows where it can, and
the last picture where it cannot (profile 5: better than nothing). A profile 5 stream that starts
without metadata still shows nothing until its first reconstructed picture: its base layer is not a
picture, and before the first picture of the video nothing else is on the screen either.

The player information no longer says that a reconstructed picture is shown for such a frame.

The rules are tested on the host (gap_policy_test.cpp, 8 checks, 5 mutations noticed); the renderer
and the window system are only compiled (syntax) and read: Kodi does not run its GUI on the host.
