+/*!
+ * \brief Hades: the base layer of a Dolby Vision stream is known to be a picture by itself: the
+ *        record of the stream gives its profile, and it is not one whose base layer is no picture
+ *        (BaseLayerIsNoPicture()). A stream whose profile is not known (0) is not taken to be one.
+ */
+constexpr bool BaseLayerIsKnownPicture(int profile, int compatibility)
+{
+  return profile > 0 && !BaseLayerIsNoPicture(profile, compatibility);
+}
+
+/*!
+ * \brief Hades: whether a picture of a stream that is reconstructed and sent as HDR10, when nothing
+ *        reconstructed can be shown for it, is shown from its base layer by Kodi's own way
+ *
+ * Nothing reconstructed can be shown when the picture comes without its Dolby Vision metadata or
+ * its reconstruction fails, and no picture reconstructed earlier may stand in for it
+ * (ConversionRepeats()): the first pictures of a stream may come without their metadata, and so
+ * may those after a seek in a stream of two tracks, until the enhancement layer starts again.
+ * Without this, nothing of the video was drawn for them. The base layer is shown only where it is
+ * the picture that the output is set up for: a picture by itself (BaseLayerIsKnownPicture()) coded
+ * with the PQ transfer in BT.2020, sent as it is to the HDR10 output that the reconstruction set
+ * up; and not where the reconstruction is mapped to the display (projectors), whose base layer
+ * would go out unmapped. Never profile 5, whose base layer would show wrong colours.
+ * \param baseIsPicture BaseLayerIsKnownPicture() of the stream (VideoPicture::doviBaseIsPicture)
+ * \param pq the picture is coded with the PQ transfer
+ * \param bt2020 ... in BT.2020 primaries
+ * \param mapped the reconstruction is mapped to the display (dvbridge_hdr10_mapping::enabled)
+ */
+constexpr bool ConversionShowsBase(bool baseIsPicture, bool pq, bool bt2020, bool mapped)
+{
+  return baseIsPicture && pq && bt2020 && !mapped;
+}
+
+/*!
+ * \brief Hades: whether the last picture that was reconstructed whole is shown again in place of
+ *        one that could not be reconstructed (it came without its metadata, or its reconstruction
+ *        failed)
+ *
+ * Within the same run of the stream, as native output does with such a picture: a picture or a
+ * few without their metadata are a still of the one before them, not a change of the grade. After
+ * a seek (another run: the decoder was flushed, VideoPicture::doviSourceEpoch), that picture is of
+ * another place in the film: the base layer is shown where it can be (ConversionShowsBase()), else
+ * that last picture all the same, which is better than nothing (profile 5).
+ * \param sameRun the picture is of the run of the stream that the last reconstructed one was of
+ *        (the decoder tells the runs apart in a stream with an enhancement layer; in any other
+ *        stream every picture counts as of the same run)
+ * \param showsBase ConversionShowsBase() of the picture
+ */
+constexpr bool ConversionRepeats(bool sameRun, bool showsBase)
+{
+  return sameRun || !showsBase;
+}
